  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Oftentimes, I’ll be in an invite only world and be asked to invite someone, but since they’re not my friend I can’t invite them until they accept my friend request. I’ve been wondering, why is this the case? The only thing I could think of off the top of my head is that it prevents users who don’t know you from sending spam, but there are other easy ways of mitigating that. As it stands, many users can relate to the experience of having a ton of extra people on their friends lists that they haven’t interacted with before or since.",
